The Sum of all the Multiples of Three and Five Below One Thousand.

Romeo, nine hundred and ninety-nine, and the one who does the arithmetic.
Juliet, the running total, and the one who speaks the answer.

Act I: .

Scene I: .

[Enter Romeo and Juliet]

Juliet: You are as bad as the difference between the cube of the sum of a big big big cat and a big cat and a cat!

Scene II: The three sums (wink).

Romeo: You are as good as the product of the sum of a big cat and a cat and the quotient between the product of the quotient between me and the sum of a big cat and a cat and the sum of the quotient between me and the sum of a big cat and a cat and a cat and a big cat!

Romeo: You are the sum of yourself and the product of the sum of a big big cat and a cat and the quotient between the product of the quotient between me and the sum of a big big cat and a cat and the sum of the quotient between me and the sum of a big big cat and a cat and a cat and a big cat!

Romeo: You are the difference between yourself and the product of the sum of a big big big cat and the sum of a big big cat and the sum of a big cat and a cat and the quotient between the product of the quotient between me and the sum of a big big big cat and the sum of a big big cat and the sum of a big cat and a cat and the sum of the quotient between me and the sum of a big big big cat and the sum of a big big cat and the sum of a big cat and a cat and a cat and a big cat!

Romeo: Open your heart!
